  "(The boy from three doors down pelts along the lane toward you, dust to his knees.) You went out on the road too! I saw you, behind the twenty from Iṣṭahbánát! He is here! The Siyyid is here!": "（隔三户人家的那个男孩沿着巷子朝你飞奔而来，尘土一直溅到膝盖。）你也出城上路了！我看见你了，就在那二十个伊斯塔赫巴纳特人后面！他到了！赛义德到了！",
  "(A broad man sits by the gate, a great iron key on a cord round his neck.) Keeper of the gate. Vaḥíd gave me the key with his own hand. I have never carried anything so heavy.": "（一个魁梧的男人坐在门边，脖子上用绳子挂着一把沉重的铁钥匙。）我是守门人。瓦希德亲手把钥匙交给了我。我从未扛过这样沉重的东西。",
  "(A man at a writing-board, ink to the wrist.) Vaḥíd has given each of us a charge. A keeper of the gate, a keeper of the purse, a reader, a gaoler with no prisoner. Mine is to write down what happens. I am the chronicler of a fort.": "（一个男人伏在书写板前，墨迹一直染到手腕。）瓦希德给我们每个人都分派了职责。有守门人，有管钱袋的，有诵读者，还有一个没有囚犯的狱卒。我的职责是记下发生的一切。我是一座堡垒的记事者。",
  "(The boy's mother stands in her doorway with a water-jug on her hip, watching the lane fill.) Neighbour's son, you have the road on you like everyone else. Drink first. Your own mother is still at the edge of the town, shouting herself hoarse.": "（那男孩的母亲腰间挎着水罐站在门口，看着巷子里人越来越多。）邻家的孩子，你和大家一样一身风尘。先喝水。你母亲还在城边呢，喊得嗓子都哑了。",
  "(An old man in a white turban leans on his staff beside the masjid door, letting the young push past.) Eighty years I have walked to this door. Today I could not get near it for the crowd. God be praised for a crowd.": "（一位头缠白巾的老人拄着手杖，立在清真寺门边，任由年轻人从身旁挤过。）八十年来，我一直走向这扇门。今天人太多，我竟挨不近它。感谢神，竟有这样的人潮。",
  "(Climb down and dig.)": "（爬下去，挖。）",
